# Proxy API + uploads to the backend so the browser only ever talks to the same
# HTTPS origin (Netlify forwards server-side). This avoids the browser blocking the
# http:// backend as "mixed content" and sidesteps CORS.
# ⚠️ To switch backends, change the target URL on these two lines and redeploy.
/api/*       http://32.236.114.49:3006/api/:splat       200
/uploads/*   http://32.236.114.49:3006/uploads/:splat   200

# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback. MUST stay last — any request that doesn't
# match a real file, the API proxy, or a _headers rule is served index.html so React
# Router can resolve client-side routes.
/*    /index.html   200
